worktree>, \"path\": \"LOGBOOK.md\", \"sha256\": <hex sha256 of the full replacement file content>, \"content\": <base64 of that content>}`; binding to any other OID is refused as \"outside the original sequence\"; every checkpoint whose replay conflicts needs its own resolution, and the replacement content at each step keeps EVERY entry (trunk's newer entries first, then the replayed checkpoint's entry, then older ones — newest-first by wall time), everything else byte-identical. Do exactly this from inside this run: (1) git fetch origin; run `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-2x16gz`; when it stops with `UU LOGBOOK.md`, inspect the retained replay worktree (`git -C <replay>/worktree rev-parse REBASE_HEAD` names the original checkpoint; the conflicted file shows HEAD = trunk side, theirs = the checkpoint's entry), build the resolved content, append the resolution to your resolutions.json and rerun `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-2x16gz --replay-resolutions <file>`; repeat for each conflicting checkpoint until `refresh_advanced`; (2) verify: the Story branch tip is the replayed last checkpoint whose parent chain reaches e4e3e8834675cf3814effd3b2673b4931dfbf311, every replayed commit signed (git verify-commit), and for each replayed checkpoint `git diff <original> <replayed> --stat` is empty except LOGBOOK.md; (3) reconcile the carried uncommitted candidate against the new base by hand, never by wholesale checkout — the carried candidate copies of trunk-changed files are STALE (they were written before the refresh): for every path in `git diff --name-only 62d446304391af187c417a88a2e14012b467956e e4e3e8834675cf3814effd3b2673b4931dfbf311` that also appears in your `git status`, diff it against HEAD and restore trunk's content (`git checkout HEAD -- <path>` only for paths that are not candidate paths; for candidate paths such as LOGBOOK.md, README.md, internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json, traceability.go, traceability_test.go, tracecheck main_test.go merge by hand so that trunk's lines are all present and your additions remain — the diff against HEAD must be purely additive for LOGBOOK/README apart from figure lines you rewrite, and the ownership registry must contain trunk's rows plus yours); task-board.config.json must equal HEAD (or HEAD plus only what your Story's earlier checkpoints intentionally carry — state which); recompute and re-pin reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 over the merged registry, refresh the tracecheck/report pins and README figures; (4) rerun the full 26-command suite from the worktree's task-board.config.json plus your own suites; (5) verify `git status` shows exactly your candidate paths (no __pycache__/.pyc), attach UPDATED outcomes TASK-260830-2x16gz_results-rev2.md (the refresh/reconcile record with exact commands, OIDs, every resolution's checkpoint binding, the stale-copy audit table path-by-path, the digest re-pin), TASK-260830-2x16gz_conformance-matrix-rev2.md and TASK-260830-2x16gz_producer-evidence-rev2.tar.gz (a real gzip archive) — a handoff without a new or updated task-scoped outcome is cancelled as handoff_unsatisfied; (6) task-board handoff TASK-260830-2x16gz --role developer and exit promptly. Do not re-implement or change product code beyond the reconciliation; never commit on the Story branch; never edit .task-board directly; never self-accept; never edit the control root. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
