{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c7a9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aeac-09f8-71f3-ab2b-385c63463936"},"sequence":559,"recorded_at":1780531400001113,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"1b8b656f-1678-46e7-bb3f-f3a0982a1bf8","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"1b8b656f-1678-46e7-bb3f-f3a0982a1bf8","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"1b8b656f-1678-46e7-bb3f-f3a0982a1bf8"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0aeae-2fc9-7de0-aecd-08b4e86595dc"},"task_id":"01a0aeae-2fc9-7de0-aecd-08b4e86595dc","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0aeae-2fc9-7de0-aecd-08b4e86595dc","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/base-refresh/replay-1191023953/worktree/LOGBOOK.md`.\n1|# Flight Logbook\n2|\n3|> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n4|> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n5|\n6|## 2026-09-17\n7|\n8|<<<<<<< HEAD\n9|### TASK-260917-3lt2xv — release-agnostic cataloggen check via -adopted\n10|- CONTRACT: validation command 21 was pinned to explicit v0.6.0 inputs, so a Story re-pointing the catalog at a new revision failed construction at its own gate. The fix declares the adopted release once (`catalog.Adopted`, consumed by `Current()`) and adds a cataloggen `-adopted` mode deriving `internal/catalog/catalog.<adopted>.json` and `internal/specpin/<adopted>.lock.json` relative to `-root` (default \".\"). Mixed `-adopted` with explicit `-metadata`/`-contracts`, a missing derived input (message names the derived path), and a lock whose source release differs from adopted are refused before generation; otherwise the same Generate call and `-check`/`-output` semantics run byte-identically to the explicit form.\n11|- GATE: command 21 is now `go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check`; every other validation command unchanged. No catalog content, metadata, lock, or generated-output change.\n12|- TESTS: adopted positives, byte-identity (adopted vs explicit v0.6.0 vs committed), and all refusals driven through the production `run` entry; the configured-command test asserts the `-adopted` shape and runs it rooted at the repo. Narrowing mutants per refusal plus a byte-identity derivation mutant, all killed; harmless control SURVIVED. Both the candidate `-adopted` command and trunk's explicit command are green on the tree.\n13|- DOCS: README regenerate block and tool row document the `-adopted` form and the explicit equivalent. No behavior or availability claims added.\n14|=======\n15|### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev12 — exact interface call sites and side-effect-free binding refusal\n16|- F1: the typed Config/Host Trust Store write-path census now allowlists interface edges by exact `*types.Func` identity plus source file/line/column, not by method spelling or enclosing-function membership. The inventory covers 119 production interface calls; the four pair-writer functions additionally require a top-level fail-fast hold guard before every admitted indirect write edge. Function-valued selectors and identifiers remain fail-closed except for named table entries; no non-callee interface method values were found in the production scan.\n17|- F1 REGRESSION: `TestWritePathCensusRejectsUnlistedInterfaceCallSite` copies the module, plants real `filesystem.Rename` calls both before and after `requireHoldForConfig`, runs the real census, and proves the child rename witness executes before the census rejects both unlisted sites. The `writepath-interface-callsite-skip` mutant preserves the allowlisted method identity while dropping call-site/hold ordering, propagates its overlay into the child, and is killed by that production regression (child exit 0 under the mutant; outer test exit 1).\n18|- F2: `ensureConfigBindingLocked` validates the store-side association and target-side association before publishing either side. A rejected second handle cannot leave a target claim behind; two handles opened before first binding publish exactly one winner; an interrupted first binding repairs the missing store index on reopen. RED evidence is `.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/rebind-red-rev12.log`; the fixed production tests are `TestReviewerRefusedRebindLeavesTargetUnclaimed`, `TestCompetingFirstBindingsPublishExactlyOneAssociation`, and `TestInterruptedFirstBindingIsRepairedAfterReopen`.\n19|- MUTATION EVIDENCE: batteries rerun in full on the post-refresh final tree: Config4 1 neutral + 13 killed, Host Trust Store 1 neutral + 34 killed, 0 survivors (47 killed total, every kill exit 1 with the expected named test failing). Runs split into 9 bounded groups with `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`; per-mutant overlays/results/tables are under `.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/mutations-*-rev12post-group*` (pre-refresh partial runs under `mutations-*-rev12-*` agree). Generated `__pycache__` bytecode was removed.\n20|- VALIDATION (final tree, head `5e54874`): `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 all packages ok (4m40s); cover config 92.9/hosttrust 76.3/peeridentity 97.5/secprim 94.4/localstore 83.8; `-race` on hosttrust+config exit 0; `go vet`, `go mod tidy -diff`, gofmt, `git diff --check` clean; native + darwin/linux/windows builds exit 0; Windows test-compile + vet exit 0 (no runtime claim). F1 gate + call-site regression pass; F2 trio passes post-fix and the rebind test fails RED (exit 1) on unfixed CR11 code. Full logs and board evidence are in the rev12 outcome package.\n21|- PRESERVATION/SCOPE: base moved by managed refresh-candidate to trunk `62d446304391af187c417a88a2e14012b467956e` (replayed checkpoints `efe119a`/`5e54874`); candidate remains UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree. RPC backup/parked delta and checkpointed SSH/peer work remain outside this leaf. AC coverage remains 19 of 21 production rows; native Windows runtime ACL and downstream export/diagnostic consumers are explicit bounds. No RPC behavior, main integration, or review acceptance is claimed.\n22|\n23|## 2026-09-17\n24|\n25|### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev11 — opaque resolved pair and current negative evidence\n26|- F2: all pair-bearing production boundaries now consume the opaque `localstore.ResolvedPaths` minted by the single `localstore.ResolvePaths` resolver. `hosttrust.Open`, binding/hold validation, `JointCommit`, `LoadCoherent`, Config4 preview/apply/rollback, legacy migration, and pair writers no longer accept caller-supplied config/state tuples. The target-side binding record is authoritative; reopening a store with a derived binding but a missing target record refuses closed. The foreign-store target-binding probe is narrowing and killed by `TestWriteTempReplaceRefusesForeignStoreWithTargetBinding`.\n27|- F1: the write-path census now compares exact `*types.Func` interface-method objects and rejects unlisted interface/type-parameter calls, parenthesized callees, and method values; executable real-file witnesses cover the new shapes. The preserved-token `writepath-interface-name-heuristic` mutant runs the behavioral suite and is killed.\n28|- MUTATION EVIDENCE: current Config4 battery has 1 neutral control plus 13 unique narrowing/precision mutants, all killed (exit 1 with named production failures; `config-association-root-skip` was rerun in `part4b` and counted once). Current Host Trust Store battery has 1 neutral control plus 34 unique narrowing/precision mutants, all killed. One first-pass `hold-state-root-skip` compile failure was a harness defect; the corrected mutant rerun killed `TestHeldExclusiveRejectsForeignConfigStateRoot`, and the failed instrument run is not counted.\n29|- VALIDATION: fresh `internal/config`, `internal/localstore`, `internal/hosttrust` tests, `go test ./... -v`, `go test ./... -cover`, `go vet ./...`, native/cross `go build`, cross test compilation with `go test -exec /usr/bin/true ./... -run '^$'` for darwin/linux/windows, `go mod tidy -diff`, gofmt, and `git diff --check` pass. The ordinary cross `go test -run '^$'` execution lane is retained as an expected host-format limitation (bad CPU/exec format), not a code pass.\n30|- PRESERVATION/HANDOFF: RPC backup 15/15 and parked delta 11/11 remain byte-identical; checkpointed SSH/peer work is untouched; no RPC path was absorbed. Candidate remains UNCOMMITTED at `HEAD=305875134f8d344eb86ef926c7fbca3fed85c49d` on protected `origin/main=8626fb361c1d6b62d5f95c7be4cb33c85d4aadf3`. AC coverage remains 19 of 21 production rows; Windows runtime ACL (row 15) and downstream export/diagnostic consumers (row 21) are explicit bounds. Ready for developer-to-reviewer handoff; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\n31|\n32|### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev10 — Config4 binding and typed write-path census closed\n33|- BASE/PRESERVATION: candidate was verified on current protected AX trunk (`origin/main=8626fb361c1d6b62d5f95c7be4cb33c85d4aadf3`, worktree HEAD `305875134f8d344eb86ef926c7fbca3fed85c49d`). The 15-file RPC backup and 11-file parked RPC delta remain byte-identical; checkpointed SSH/peer work remains present and no RPC implementation path was absorbed. Candidate changes remain UNCOMMITTED for the managed Story handoff.\n34|- F1: Config4 now has an immutable, owner-only `config-binding.json` sidecar. Binding is explicit through `EnsureConfigBinding`; `JointCommit`, `LoadCoherent`, and pair writers require the existing binding and reject a missing, malformed, unreadable, rebound, or foreign state-root binding. The config-side selected `StateRoot` is compared to the canonical Host Trust Store root; no non-normative Config4 field was added to the closed `mesh.host_channel` table. `OpenForConfig` and the implicit legacy fallback were removed.\n35|- F2: the write-path census is typed and fail-closed: unresolved calls, non-`*types.Func` call targets, and unlisted object identities are rejected; only explicit receiver/method, function-field, parameter/local, package-initializer, and external helper allowlists are accepted. New controls cover type-parameter method values, channel callbacks, and immediate function literals. The token-preserving `writepath-method-value-skip` mutant executes the behavioral suite and is killed.\n36|- MUTATION EVIDENCE: Config4 battery has 1 neutral control passed and 11 narrowing/precision mutants killed; Host Trust Store battery has 1 neutral control passed and 34 narrowing/precision mutants killed, with zero survivors. Results are archived under `.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/mutations-config-final/` and the `mutations-hosttrust-rev10-*` directories. Initial relative-`GOCACHE` setup failures are retained as setup failures and are not counted as kills.\n37|- VALIDATION: `go test ./... -count=1 -v` and `go test ./... -count=1 -cover` passed for all 26 packages; touched-package race tests, `go vet`, native and Windows cross-builds, Windows test compilation/vet, `go mod tidy -diff`, catalog generation check, tracecheck, gofmt, and diff-check passed. Darwin custody runtime is covered; Windows ACL runtime and downstream export/diagnostic consumers remain stated bounds, not invented passes. Exact logs and the write-path census are attached in the rev10 outcome package.\n38|- AC: 19 of 21 enumerated production acceptance rows are driven by named production-entry tests and pass. Rows 15 (Windows runtime ACL equivalence) and 21 (consumer/diagnostic export surfaces outside this repository) remain explicit bounds. This is the accepted scope boundary; RPC/TLS/hello/dispatch/stream lifecycle remains with its owning task.\n39|- HANDOFF: outcome evidence is ready for independent review. This entry does not claim review acceptance, main integration, or delivery.\n40|\n41|## 2026-09-16\n42|\n43|### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev7 — CR6 transaction-family findings repaired at the type level\n44|- F1: `migrate` runs inside the authorization transaction (`openLegacyStore` + `WithExclusiveHold` + `revalidateLegacySource` + token-gated `replaceDurably`): legacy writers serialize with joint commits and refuse `ErrMigrationStaleSource` when the source moved. Rev6 unlocked exemption deleted; pre-hold refusals write nothing; opening creates the owner-only skeleton when absent (documented) and fails closed when unopenable. Sync CR6 probe RED pre-fix; post-fix it blocks on the held lock (timeout dump proves the hold, CR5-restore precedent) and the committed async port `TestLegacyMigrateCannotOverwriteCommittedV4` pins serialize-then-refuse-stale + fresh Config4 commit.\n45|- F2: `JointCommit` routes replace errors through `resolveFailedReplace` (pin-verified: source-intact aborts with the original error, durable/diverged/unreadable runs compensation restore-or-keep-marker). Both CR6 probes RED pre-fix, green post-fix; marker-kept reopen/forward tests added for apply + rollback (`TestApplyV4FailedReplaceKeepsMarkerWhenRestoreFails` + rollback twin, `TestResolveFailedReplaceKeepsMarker`).\n46|- F3/INSTRUMENT: `hosttrust.HeldExclusive` capability (only `exclusiveHold` forges; verified live pre-write; expired on unlock) threaded through all pair writers; `store.lock.exclusive()` signature kept for read paths and probe compat. Static gate rewritten fail-closed (all decls incl. package-var initializers, transitive alias resolution, helper-escape detection, exact (receiver,method) backend pairs, direct-os-mutation rule, hold-entry closures for JointCommit+WithExclusiveHold) with 6 executable rogue controls (4 reviewer verbatim + direct-os.WriteFile + backend-receiver rogue); rev6 token-less plants no longer compile (vet error captured as evidence).\n47|- EVIDENCE: hosttrust battery 33 killed (32 narrowing + 1 call-site) + neutral passed; config 10 killed (9 semantic + 1 label-precision) + neutral passed; new plants hold-require-skip, hold-no-lock, resolve-source-skip, replace-require-skip, legacy-revalidate-skip, replace-restore-skip (each admits exactly one member; kept halves verified in plant logs). Full loca