ase c1eff01; `refresh-candidate` still refuses (\"requires the final unresolved leaf\"). No vendoring, no manual rebase. Candidate left UNCOMMITTED for snapshot.\n84|\n85|## 2026-09-10\n86|\n87|### TASK-260909-2ez769 — Host Trust Store 1.0.0 + Config 4.0.0 migration implemented\n88|- SCOPE: new `internal/hosttrust` (trust reader/writer, Profile-1 issuance/verify, custody, enroll/rotate/MarkRetiring/revoke, generation authz, export/exclusion); Config 4.0.0 reader/validator/encoder + Preview/Apply/Rollback in `internal/config`; v4 peeridentity interop test; secprim census extended to hosttrust.\n89|- FINDING: peer rotation catch-up had no local path (only self-rotation). Added `Store.MarkRetiring` with the same 24h/enrolled_at bounds. `ensureOwnerDir` verifies existing dirs, never repairs: silent narrowing masked a widened dir (caught by TestCustodyRefusals).\n90|- FINDING: Go x509 puts the CN ATV into Subject.Names (len 1), so CN-only means exactly one CN-OID ATV, not empty Names. Parsed-name check fixed in `profile_checks.go:subjectIsOnlyCN`.\n91|- FINDING: encoding/json decodes `\"1\"` into json.Number; generation now requires a bare JSON number. Duplicate JSON keys audited via token stream before decode.\n92|- DECISION: base refresh refused by tooling (\"candidate refresh requires the final unresolved leaf\"); no manual rebase. Candidate sits on c1eff01 citing v0.6.0 by value; adoption files not duplicated. Integration must land onto the adoption base.\n93|- VALIDATION: 21/21 AC rows driven; 11 hosttrust + 3 config narrowing mutants killed (named), 1 label-precision kill, 2 neutral controls; `go test ./...` all ok; config refusal-inventory + secprim census green.\n94|- STATUS: ready for review, worktree UNCOMMITTED for handoff snapshot.\n95|\n96|## 2026-09-17\n97|>>>>>>> ae5a4cc (TASK-260909-2ez769: TASK-260909-2ez769: implement-host-credentials-and-config4-migration)\n98|\n99|### TASK-260830-21gygk — rev16 rework: normalize Go aliases in the sealed-capability census\n100|- REVIEW FINDING CLOSED (CR15 P2-A): the package-wide `go/types` census\n101|  compared lexical `*types.TypeName` objects, so a Go alias could bypass the\n102|  sealed `checkpointSeal`/`checkpointSealToken` inventory. The initial alias\n103|  baseline admitted the direct, token, chained, and container plants; its\n104|  recorded exit was 1 before the fix.\n105|- FIX (`internal/sessquery/rev11_regression_test.go`): every sealed type and\n106|  value identity path now applies `types.Unalias` before canonical comparison\n107|  and before structural descent. The recursive coverage includes chained\n108|  aliases, pointers, arrays, slices, maps, channels, structs, function\n109|  signatures, generic arguments, interfaces, type parameters, and unions.\n110|  Unrelated named capability types are not opened through their underlying\n111|  representation, so the census keeps the public capability boundary intact.\n112|- TESTS (`internal/sessquery/rev15_regression_test.go`): direct, chained,\n113|  container, and function-signature alias plants all refuse through the same\n114|  production census entry. The existing callback-provenance negative now binds\n115|  its unknown callback locally inside the approved profile flow, isolating the\n116|  callback object-identity gate from the independent package-scope sealed-value\n117|  guard; its narrowing mutant is killed by the same instrument.\n118|- MUTANTS: the final local battery (`mutants-rev16b`) reports 66/66 applied N/B\n119|  plants killed (63 narrowing, 3 ordering). The applied harmless control is\n120|  `SURVIVED`; `NOT_APPLIED` and `COMPILE_OR_HARNESS_FAILURE` remain separate\n121|  classifier outcomes. The alias mutant removes `types.Unalias` only from the\n122|  nested sealed-value recursion path and fails the container plant.\n123|- CLEANUP: removed the stray `internal/sessquery/testdata/__pycache__` Python\n124|  cache from the candidate; the mutation copy restored all mutated source\n125|  bytes and the fin