 tests + 8 hosttrust compensation tests (tamper/corrupt/unreadable marker, noop+wrong-bytes restore verification, fail-after-write, source-present skip). TEST BUG FOUND BY RACE SUITE ITSELF: boundary tests deadlocked reading trust post-seam on the main goroutine — request now binds pre-seam with a comment.\n54|- EVIDENCE: hosttrust battery 29 narrowing (incl. 4 compensate-*) + 1 call-site + neutral passed; config 6 semantic + 1 label + neutral passed; all plants pre-verified count==1 with exits from subprocess return codes. Full local CI replicated green (26 ok, 0 FAIL, 1 pre-existing SKIP; race 26 ok; cover hosttrust 77.9/config 93.3; tracecheck/catalog-6/cigate-contracts-6/claims-6/targets-2/fuzz-13/fixtures 51+59 zero-skip/windows-compile). 7 original reviewer probes re-pass; rows 15/21 retained bounded per CR5.\n55|- BOUNDS RESTATED: verifyLockFile 500ms retry rechecks custody without pinning an inode (no external-replacement claim); power-loss beyond fsync unproven; Windows runtime unverified; diagnostics export unowned; spurious-bump corner aborts fail-safe.\n56|\n57|### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev5 — CR4 surviving-reader + lock-init findings repaired\n58|- F1: pending joint-commit marker is now a general admission barrier (`convergeLocked` + shared-to-exclusive dance `lockForConvergedRead`): every read/admission/transaction entry point converges or refuses before exposing a snapshot. Surviving stores converge exactly like reopened ones; stale bindings compare against the recovered generation (never refreshed). Real child-process crash tests (exit 77) cover surviving + reopened × apply + rollback, marker cleanup, and intervened refusal with marker kept.\n59|- F2: lock init is atomic non-replacing (O_CREAT|O_EXCL / CREATE_NEW via `FileSystem.CreateExclusive`); losers open the existing inode. Existing-file verify retries 500ms for the create-to-secure window; non-regular refuses immediately. Deterministic cross-process first-open test pins returnedWhileHeld=false + sameInode=true; the replacing-rename mutant restores the exact reviewer failure shape.\n60|- F3: native Windows custody tests written (7, build-tagged; vet + test-compile pass, runtime unverified); config backups classified (byte-exact config copies, 0600, excluded names; Windows backup DACLs a stated bound); row-21 handoff persisted with per-surface API/test obligations + notes on all 7 owned tasks, diagnostics explicitly unowned.\n61|- MUTANT LESSON: a JointCommit converge-ignore mutant survives because the staged-marker refusal backstops it — error-ignoring mutants are unobservable where a file-level backstop stands. Paired instead: joint-converge-skip (call-site, killed) + recover-forward-no-bump (narrowing, kills 8 named convergence tests).\n62|- EVIDENCE: hosttrust battery 25 narrowing + 1 call-site killed + neutral passed; config 4 semantic + 1 label + neutral passed; full local CI replicated green (test/race/cover/tracecheck/catalog/cigate/fuzz-13/fixtures/claims/windows-compile). 19 of 21 AC rows driven; rows 15 (Windows runtime) and 21 (consumers) bounded, not passed.\n63|\n64|## 2026-09-10 (refresh)\n65|\n66|### TASK-260909-2ez769 refresh — story base moved c1eff01 to a89328c (trunk 8cf4aaa + v0.6.0 adoption)\n67|- REFRESH: `task-board worktree refresh-candidate` with exclusive lease (RUN-260910-a4ac2c). Round 1 (43c0e2b peer-identity): 5 file resolutions — LOGBOOK merged newest-first, README trunk + peer tail, 3 traceability files trunk-wins (v0.6.0 registry pin authoritative; v0.5.0 digest superseded). Round 2 (c1eff01 SSH): 4 resolutions reusing round-1 bytes + README with SSH `## SSH stdio transport` section appended and peer-section wording. Packet schema learned from tool errors: entries {checkpoint_oid, path, sha256, content-base64}. Both replayed commits signed oparin@me.com (41106b6, a89328c, verify-commit Good).\n68|- COMBINE: worktree restored to candidate snapshot by tool; 30 enumerated incoming paths restored from HEAD (8 adoption files