{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c7d3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aeac-09f8-71f3-ab2b-385c63463936"},"sequence":580,"recorded_at":1780531400001155,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"1b8b656f-1678-46e7-bb3f-f3a0982a1bf8","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"1b8b656f-1678-46e7-bb3f-f3a0982a1bf8","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"1b8b656f-1678-46e7-bb3f-f3a0982a1bf8"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0aeae-886c-7540-8c7b-4a833c3aeda4"},"task_id":"01a0aeae-886c-7540-8c7b-4a833c3aeda4","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0aeae-886c-7540-8c7b-4a833c3aeda4","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-20-1\",\n  \"command\": \"R=/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/base-refresh/replay-1191023953/worktree; echo \\\"===OURS(HEAD/trunk) head===\\\"; git -C $R show :2:LOGBOOK.md 2>/dev/null | head -n 25; echo; echo \\\"===THEIRS(checkpoint) head===\\\"; git -C $R show :3:LOGBOOK.md 2>/dev/null | head -n 35; echo; echo \\\"===BASE head===\\\"; git -C $R show :1:LOGBOOK.md 2>/dev/null | head -n 20\",\n  \"description\": \"Show three conflict versions of LOGBOOK\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"===OURS(HEAD/trunk) head===\\n# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-17\\n\\n### TASK-260917-3lt2xv — release-agnostic cataloggen check via -adopted\\n- CONTRACT: validation command 21 was pinned to explicit v0.6.0 inputs, so a Story re-pointing the catalog at a new revision failed construction at its own gate. The fix declares the adopted release once (`catalog.Adopted`, consumed by `Current()`) and adds a cataloggen `-adopted` mode deriving `internal/catalog/catalog.<adopted>.json` and `internal/specpin/<adopted>.lock.json` relative to `-root` (default \\\".\\\"). Mixed `-adopted` with explicit `-metadata`/`-contracts`, a missing derived input (message names the derived path), and a lock whose source release differs from adopted are refused before generation; otherwise the same Generate call and `-check`/`-output` semantics run byte-identically to the explicit form.\\n- GATE: command 21 is now `go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check`; every other validation command unchanged. No catalog content, metadata, lock, or generated-output change.\\n- TESTS: adopted positives, byte-identity (adopted vs explicit v0.6.0 vs committed), and all refusals driven through the production `run` entry; the configured-command test asserts the `-adopted` shape and runs it rooted at the repo. Narrowing mutants per refusal plus a byte-identity derivation mutant, all killed; harmless control SURVIVED. Both the candidate `-adopted` command and trunk's explicit command are green on the tree.\\n- DOCS: README regenerate block and tool row document the `-adopted` form and the explicit equivalent. No behavior or availability claims added.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-21gygk — rev16 rework: normalize Go aliases in the sealed-capability census\\n- REVIEW FINDING CLOSED (CR15 P2-A): the package-wide `go/types` census\\n  compared lexical `*types.TypeName` objects, so a Go alias could bypass the\\n  sealed `checkpointSeal`/`checkpointSealToken` inventory. The initial alias\\n  baseline admitted the direct, token, chained, and container plants; its\\n  recorded exit was 1 before the fix.\\n- FIX (`internal/sessquery/rev11_regression_test.go`): every sealed type and\\n  value identity path now applies `types.Unalias` before canonical comparison\\n  and before structural descent. The recursive coverage includes chained\\n  aliases, pointers, arrays, slices, maps, channels, structs, function\\n  signatures, generic arguments, interfaces, type parameters, and unions.\\n  Unrelated named capability types are not opened through their underlying\\n\\n===THEIRS(checkpoint) head===\\n# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-17\\n\\n### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev12 — exact interface call sites and side-effect-free binding refusal\\n- F1: the typed Config/Host Trust Store write-path census now allowlists interface edges by exact `*types.Func` identity plus source file/line/column, not by method spelling or enclosing-function membership. The inventory covers 119 production interface calls; the four pair-writer functions additionally require a top-level fail-fast hold guard before every admitted indirect write edge. Function-valued selectors and identifiers remain fail-closed except for named table entries; no non-callee interface method values were found in the production scan.\\n- F1 REGRESSION: `TestWritePathCensusRejectsUnlistedInterfaceCallSite` copies the module, plants real `filesystem.Rename` calls both before and after `requireHoldForConfig`, runs the real census, and proves the child rename witness executes before the census rejects both unlisted sites. The `writepath-interface-callsite-skip` mutant preserves the allowlisted method identity while dropping call-site/hold ordering, propagates its overlay into the child, and is killed by that production regression (child exit 0 under the mutant; outer test exit 1).\\n- F2: `ensureConfigBindingLocked` validates the store-side association and target-side association before publishing either side. A rejected second handle cannot leave a target claim behind; two handles opened before first binding publish exactly one winner; an interrupted first binding repairs the missing store index on reopen. RED evidence is `.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/rebind-red-rev12.log`; the fixed production tests are `TestReviewerRefusedRebindLeavesTargetUnclaimed`, `TestCompetingFirstBindingsPublishExactlyOneAssociation`, and `TestInterruptedFirstBindingIsRepairedAfterReopen`.\\n- MUTATION EVIDENCE: batteries rerun in full on the post-refresh final tree: Config4 1 neutral + 13 killed, Host Trust Store 1 neutral + 34 killed, 0 survivors (47 killed total, every kill exit 1 with the expected named test failing). Runs split into 9 bounded groups with `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`; per-mutant overlays/results/tables are under `.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/mutations-*-rev12post-group*` (pre-refresh partial runs under `mutations-*-rev12-*` agree). Generated `__pycache__` bytecode was removed.\\n- VALIDATION (final tree, head `5e54874`): `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 all packages ok (4m40s); cover config 92.9/hosttrust 76.3/peeridentity 97.5/secprim 94.4/localstore 83.8; `-race` on hosttrust+config exit 0; `go vet`, `go mod tidy -diff`, gofmt, `git diff --check` clean; native + darwin/linux/windows builds exit 0; Windows test-compile + vet exit 0 (no runtime claim). F1 gate + call-site regression pass; F2 trio passes post-fix and the rebind test fails RED (exit 1) on unfixed CR11 code. Full logs and board evidence are in the rev12 outcome package.\\n- PRESERVATION/SCOPE: base moved by managed refresh-candidate to trunk `62d446304391af187c417a88a2e14012b467956e` (replayed checkpoints `efe119a`/`5e54874`); candidate remains UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree. RPC backup/parked delta and checkpointed SSH/peer work remain outside this leaf. AC coverage remains 19 of 21 production rows; native Windows runtime ACL and downstream export/diagnostic consumers are explicit bounds. No RPC behavior, main integration, or review acceptance is claimed.\\n\\n## 2026-09-17\\n\\n### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev11 — opaque resolved pair and current negative evidence\\n- F2: all pair-bearing production boundaries now consume the opaque `localstore.ResolvedPaths` minted by the single `localstore.ResolvePaths` resolver. `hosttrust.Open`, binding/hold validation, `JointCommit`, `LoadCoherent`, Config4 preview/apply/rollback, legacy migration, and pair writers no longer accept caller-supplied config/state tuples. The target-side binding record is authoritative; reopening a store with a derived binding but a missing target record refuses closed. The foreign-store target-binding probe is narrowing and killed by `TestWriteTempReplaceRefusesForeignStoreWithTargetBinding`.\\n- F1: the write-path census now compares exact `*types.Func` interface-method objects and rejects unlisted interface/type-parameter calls, parenthesized callees, and method values; executable real-file witnesses cover the new shapes. The preserved-token `writepath-interface-name-heuristic` mutant runs the behavioral suite and is killed.\\n- MUTATION EVIDENCE: current Config4 battery has 1 neutral control plus 13 unique narrowing/precision mutants, all killed (exit 1 with named production failures; `config-association-root-skip` was rerun in `part4b` and counted once). Current Host Trust Store battery has 1 neutral control plus 34 unique narrowing/precision mutants, all killed. One first-pass `hold-state-root-skip` compile failure was a harness defect; the corrected mutant rerun killed `TestHeldExclusiveRejectsForeignConfigStateRoot`, and the failed instrument run is not counted.\\n- VALIDATION: fresh `internal/config`, `internal/localstore`, `internal/hosttrust` tests, `go test ./... -v`, `go test ./... -cover`, `go vet ./...`, native/cross `go build`, cross test compilation with `go test -exec /usr/bin/true ./... -run '^$'` for darwin/linux/windows, `go mod tidy -diff`, gofmt, and `git diff --check` pass. The ordinary cross `go test -run '^$'` execution lane is retained as an expected host-format limitation (bad CPU/exec format), not a code pass.\\n- PRESERVATION/HANDOFF: RPC backup 15/15 and parked delta 11/11 remain byte-identical; checkpointed SSH/peer work is untouched; no RPC path was absorbed. Candidate remains UNCOMMITTED at `HEAD=305875134f8d344eb86ef926c7fbca3fed85c49d` on protected `origin/main=8626fb361c1d6b62d5f95c7be4cb33c85d4aadf3`. AC coverage remains 