{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c8c1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aeac-09f8-71f3-ab2b-385c63463936"},"sequence":699,"recorded_at":1780531400001393,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"1b8b656f-1678-46e7-bb3f-f3a0982a1bf8","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"1b8b656f-1678-46e7-bb3f-f3a0982a1bf8","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"1b8b656f-1678-46e7-bb3f-f3a0982a1bf8"},"call_id":"call_01a0aeaf4603752a92a156fdc94dda9f","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-24-1\",\n  \"command\": \"cd /tmp/republish-2x16gz && diff base_tail.txt theirs_tail.txt | head -n 40; echo \\\"===DIFFSTAT===\\\"; diff base_tail.txt theirs_tail.txt | grep -c '^[<>]'\",\n  \"description\": \"Locate tail differences precisely\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"1862a1863,1892\\n> \\n> ## 2026-09-10 (later)\\n> \\n> ### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework — CR3 changes-requested repaired on base a89328c\\n> - SCOPE: same candidate, no base move (adoption trunk already in). All five CR3 findings addressed in `internal/hosttrust` + `internal/config`; no RPC absorption (4 tracked RPC paths verified CLEAN, parked 11/11 intact, no rpcwire remnants).\\n> - P1 STALE MUTATION: `WithMutationAuthorization` no longer refreshes the cached generation; a binding older than committed refuses `ErrStaleGeneration` (`authorize.go`). Committed `TestWithMutationAuthorizationRefusesStaleGeneration` + narrowing plant `stale-mutation-refresh` (KILLED).\\n> - P1 BOUNDARY/REVOKE: lock descriptors are per-acquisition (unix `flock`, Windows `LockFileEx`), so same-process goroutines serialize like separate processes; lock-file creation guarded by a process mutex; `Initialize` no longer re-acquires (unlocked nested read + documented no-reentry discipline). Existing serialization test hardened to the deterministic 250ms contention shape. Narrowing coverage via `revoke-state` + serialization tests.\\n> - P1 CRASH ATOMICITY: new joint commit (`joint.go`): closed `PendingCommit` marker, `JointCommit` (in-lock revalidation + marker + replace + bump + unmark), `Recover` (forward/abort/refuse) auto-run by `Open`. `CommitConfigChange` removed (it encoded the split-brain pattern). Apply/rollback revalidate preview/source/generation/custody inside the exclusive hold; post-bump failures restore source + converge via `Recover` (`ErrJointReplacementDurable`). Committed real child-process crash test (`TestApplyV4CrashConvergesGeneration`, exit 77) plus abort/intervention/already-bumped/exhaustion unit tests. Power-loss vs process-crash documented honestly (fsync-durable, disk-dependent).\\n> - P1 WINDOWS DACL: `verifyOwner` now audits owner SID plus every DACL allow entry (null/empty/deny-only/unknown-type fail closed); creation paths install protected owner-only DACLs (`secureStaged`); Unix mode checks abstracted via `platformModeOK` (exact 0700/0600 preserved). Pure `ownerOnlyGrants` evaluator tested on darwin (9 cases). No Windows runner exists here: evidence is GOOS=windows build + vet clean, unit tests, and an explicit stated bound (no invented runtime pass).\\n> - P2 EXCLUSION: `ExcludedFromReplication` gains the joint marker; new `MatchExcludedFromReplication` (staging prefixes, fail-closed escapes) and `ExcludedConfigDirName` (.bak./.pre-rollback./.ax-config-*) with custody-walk + published-backup-name tests. No in-repo replication/snapshot/export-of-state surface exists (sessadapter/localstore/dirnode do not touch host-channel); outcome hands consumers + required tests to future export surfaces. Config claim corrected: 4 semantic narrowing + 1 label-precision kill (label plant marked LABEL-PRECISION in-table).\\n> - ROW 13: new production `LoadCoherent` (config+trust under one shared hold) + serialization test.\\n> - VALIDATION (rerun this run, exit 0): gofmt clean; `go vet ./...`; `go test ./... -count=1` all ok (281 top-level PASS across hosttrust/config/peeridentity/secprim); `-cover` hosttrust 77.8 config 93.1 peeridentity 97.5 secprim 94.4; `-race` on hosttrust+config ok; tracecheck ok; catalog v0.6.0 -check ok; linux+windows amd64 builds ok; `git diff --check` clean; refusal-inventory audit green (new sites covered by direct revalidation/helper tests); census green. Mutation batteries rerun exact-source: hosttrust 18 narrowing KILLED + neutral passed; config 4 semantic + 1 label KILLED + neutral passed (manifests bound to a89328c in mutations-*-rework/).\\n> - STATUS: ready for review, worktree UNCOMMITTED for handoff snapshot. `task-board validate` shows 231 pre-existing board-wide ledger-mirror issues, none referencing this task.\\n> \\n> ### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev8 — CR7 resource binding and typed write-path census\\n> - BASE: managed `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260909-2ez769` advanced the candidate to protected AX trunk `8626fb361c1d6b62d5f95c7be4cb33c85d4aadf3`, replaying the checkpointed SSH/peer leaves. The RPC backup manifest and parked RPC delta remain preserved; no RPC implementation path was absorbed. Candidate branch head is `305875134f8d344eb86ef926c7fbca3fed85c49d` and remains uncommitted.\\n> - FIX (F2): `HeldExclusive` now carries the exact trust-store root/lock identity and an explicit configuration-path binding. `requireHoldForRoot` protects hosttrust mutations; `ValidateConfigPath` protects Config4/legacy pair writes; `JointCommit` binds the marker path before replace/restore callbacks; legacy migration uses `WithExclusiveHoldForConfig`. A genuine hold from a different Store refuses before staging while the target lock is live (`TestWriteTempReplaceRefusesForeignStoreHold`). Zero, released, same-store, and unbound live holds are all production-position negative tests.\\n> - FIX (F1): the Config/Host Trust Store write-path gate now loads production packages with `golang.org/x/tools/go/packages` and resolves `go/types` objects by package path, receiver, and me