ction interface calls; the four pair-writer functions additionally require a top-level fail-fast hold guard before every admitted indirect write edge. Function-valued selectors and identifiers remain fail-closed except for named table entries; no non-callee interface method values were found in the production scan.\\n> - F1 REGRESSION: `TestWritePathCensusRejectsUnlistedInterfaceCallSite` copies the module, plants real `filesystem.Rename` calls both before and after `requireHoldForConfig`, runs the real census, and proves the child rename witness executes before the census rejects both unlisted sites. The `writepath-interface-callsite-skip` mutant preserves the allowlisted method identity while dropping call-site/hold ordering, propagates its overlay into the child, and is killed by that production regression (child exit 0 under the mutant; outer test exit 1).\\n> - F2: `ensureConfigBindingLocked` validates the store-side association and target-side association before publishing either side. A rejected second handle cannot leave a target claim behind; two handles opened before first binding publish exactly one winner; an interrupted first binding repairs the missing store index on reopen. RED evidence is `.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/rebind-red-rev12.log`; the fixed production tests are `TestReviewerRefusedRebindLeavesTargetUnclaimed`, `TestCompetingFirstBindingsPublishExactlyOneAssociation`, and `TestInterruptedFirstBindingIsRepairedAfterReopen`.\\n> - MUTATION EVIDENCE: batteries rerun in full on the post-refresh final tree: Config4 1 neutral + 13 killed, Host Trust Store 1 neutral + 34 killed, 0 survivors (47 killed total, every kill exit 1 with the expected named test failing). Runs split into 9 bounded groups with `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`; per-mutant overlays/results/tables are under `.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/mutations-*-rev12post-group*` (pre-refresh partial runs under `mutations-*-rev12-*` agree). Generated `__pycache__` bytecode was removed.\\n> - VALIDATION 